    "answer": "SBI Shaurya is a special education loan only for wards and spouses of Defence (Army, Navy, Air Force), Indian Coast Guard and Central Armed Police Force personnel. You can borrow up to ₹40 lakh for studies in India and up to ₹1.5 crore for studies abroad. The co-borrower (parent) must hold a Diamond or Platinum Defence Salary Package (DSP) or Indian Coast Guard Salary Package (ICGSP) account with SBI, and that salary/pension account must stay with SBI for the whole loan period. Interest (effective 09 June 2026, as published by SBI): 8.65% a year for studies in India and abroad above ₹7.5 lakh, 8.15% with security at select institutions abroad, with a 0.50% concession for girl students. No collateral is needed up to ₹7.5 lakh. Moratorium is the course period plus 1 year, or 6 months after getting a job, whichever is earlier; repayment up to 15 years. It covers tuition, hostel, books, laptop, travel, insurance, and a two-wheeler up to ₹50,000 when collateral is given. Note: some guides quote 10.15–11.75% — rates differ by loan category and change often, so confirm the current rate on sbi.co.in or at the branch before applying.",
